# Physics Foundations Manifest

Use this document to guide baseline simulation fidelity for Codex physics generation. Includes canonical principles, real-world models, and public formula libraries.

---

## ⚛️ Fundamental Constants & Laws

**Name:** NIST Physical Constants\
**Type:** US Gov Database\
**URL:** [https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Constants/](https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Constants/)

Use: Gravity, force equations, thermodynamic laws, universal values

---

## 📐 Motion & Force Libraries

**Name:** The Feynman Lectures on Physics\
**Type:** Public Archive\
**URL:** [https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/](https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/)

Use: Newtonian mechanics, momentum transfer, stress analysis foundations

---

## 🌊 Fluid & Pressure Simulation

**Name:** MIT Fluids Engineering Resources\
**Type:** Courseware + Sim Docs\
**URL:** [https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mechanical-engineering/2-25-advanced-fluid-mechanics-fall-2013/](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mechanical-engineering/2-25-advanced-fluid-mechanics-fall-2013/)

Use: Particle movement under pressure, blood/acid modeling, explosive force propagation

